WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:03.640
In the UK, a couple can
marry in a register office,

2
00:00:03.690 --> 00:00:05.580
without a single prayer.

3
00:00:05.630 --> 00:00:10.220
In law, that wedding counts just as
much as one in a place of worship.

4
00:00:10.270 --> 00:00:13.260
And many couples now live
together without marrying at all,

5
00:00:13.310 --> 00:00:15.510
or choose a civil partnership.

6
00:00:15.560 --> 00:00:19.620
So why do so many religions make
marriage a promise before God,

7
00:00:19.670 --> 00:00:21.920
not just a legal contract?

8
00:00:21.970 --> 00:00:25.270
In this mission, you will
explore the purposes of marriage,

9
00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:28.550
starting from Jesus' words in Mark 10.

10
00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:31.220
Then you will compare
views on living together,

11
00:00:31.270 --> 00:00:34.680
and weigh up whether
marriage still matters today.

12
00:00:34.730 --> 00:00:40.120
Your mission: explain why so many religions
make marriage a promise before God.
